---
term: Constitutional authority
section: evolution-and-protection
order: 10
definition: The power to create, interpret, and amend a charter. In the Social Charter, this authority belongs to the corporation's members.
seeAlso:
  - living-charter
  - executive-agent
---
Members keep constitutional authority and delegate other functions, such as execution and measurement, to commissions of the charter. See [[delegation of functions]].
